@startuml paired_consent_rotation
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title Paired Consent Rotation Sequence Diagram

box "User Side" #AliceBlue
actor User order 1 #LightCyan
participant Iso order 2 #LightBlue
participant Boomlet order 3 #LightPink
participant ST order 4 #Violet
participant Boomletwo order 5 #LightGray
participant Niso order 6 #LightGreen
end box
participant WT order 98 #Red
participant SAR order 99 #Yellow

autonumber "<b>[00]"
|||

note over ST, Boomletwo #LightYellow
  PairBinding and its normal-key certificate are provisioned and retained.
  Source and target have separate management keys; the logical peer key is copied.
  ST retains its logical Boomlet pairing, setup ID, normal key, pair digest and generation.
  Both consent records and prior decision floors match before a new attempt.
  No withdrawal, signing handoff, outstanding check, or SAR duty may be unresolved.
end note

note over Iso, Boomletwo #Lavender
  ENC = SPEC cbc_cmac_encrypt; DEC authenticates before decryption.
  SIG = SPEC sign_message; VERIFY checks exact signer, domain and content type.
  DOM(op) = "Boomerang/consent_rotation/v1/" + fixed_operation.
  CTX(op) = canonical_encode("consent_rotation_" + fixed_operation, setup_id).
  LCTX(op) = canonical_encode("consent_rotation_" + fixed_ST_operation).
  E_BW(op,P) = ENC(k_BW, CTX(op), SIG(B_management, DOM(op), P)).
  E_WB(op,P) = ENC(k_WB, CTX(op), SIG(W_management, DOM(op), P)).
  k_BW and k_WB use certified physical keys, roles, direction and PROTOCOL_VERSION.
  ST encryption uses the existing directional logical Boomlet/ST keys.
  EH(E) = sha256(canonical_encode(E)); CD(C) hashes the canonical Candidate.
  Frame(op,E) uses the fixed selector, u16 envelope length and zero transport padding.
  Every fresh envelope uses a fresh IV. Retries preserve exact bytes.
end note

note over Boomlet, Boomletwo #LightYellow
  Every receive checks bounded framing, expected context, canonical payload,
  exact scope, authorized sender, operation, attempt floor and journal phase.
  Invalid input preserves authority holds and duress; failures are uniform.
  Every response uses a trusted receipt-relative fixed release deadline.
  Durable state and exact reply are stored before release.
  Iso relays ceremony envelopes unchanged; devices enforce authorization and timing.
  ST retains its air-gapped interface.
end note

group Trusted review and normal-key authorization

  ' Step 1
  User o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoInput1 \n Request consent replacement; bring Boomlet and Boomletwo into Iso
  hnote over Iso #Lavender:  Reconstruct normal key

  ' Step 2
  Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage1 \n BEGIN_REVIEW, empty canonical tuple
  hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Check current binding, resolved predecessor and bounded capacity
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Create Scope with next attempt_seq, fresh rotation_id and new_commit_id
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Create review_nonce; retain one volatile pending intent
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Review = MessageWithNonce(Scope, review_nonce)
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  E_review = ENC(k_BS, LCTX(review_challenge), (PairCertificate, Review))

  ' Step 3
  Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage1 \n (PairCertificate, Scope, E_review)

  ' Step 4
  Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage1 \n **QR**(Frame(review_challenge, E_review))
  hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; verify normal certificate, stored anchors, logical pairing and Scope

  ' Step 5
  ST o-> User:  <b>ConsentRotationStOutput1 \n **ST's Monitor**(Display consent replacement, setup, device pair and epochs)

  ' Step 6
  User o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationStInput1 \n **ST's Joystick**(Approve exact intent)
  hnote over ST #Lavender:  A_st = SIG(ST, DOM(st_review), Review)
  hnote over ST #Lavender:  E_review_approval = ENC(k_SB, LCTX(review_approval), A_st)

  ' Step 7
  ST o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationStIsoMessage1 \n **QR**(Frame(review_approval, E_review_approval))

  ' Step 8
  Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage2 \n SUBMIT_REVIEW(E_review_approval)
  hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY A_st; require pending Scope and review_nonce

  ' Step 9
  Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage2 \n Verified A_st, containing no countries or duress state
  hnote over Iso #Pink:  Verify recovered normal key, pair certificate, ST signature and exact Scope
  hnote over Iso #Lavender:  Auth = SIG(normal_key, DOM(authorize), A_st)

  ' Step 10
  Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage3 \n SUBMIT_AUTH(Auth)
  hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Verify Auth and A_st against pending intent and stored normal/ST keys
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically reserve journal, set attempt floor, quarantine predecessor, enter HOLD_WAIT
end

group Both devices held before the previous-set question
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  P_hold = (Scope, PairCertificate, Auth)
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Store E_hold = E_BW(hold, P_hold) before output

  ' Step 11
  Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage3 \n Frame(hold, E_hold)

  ' Step 12
  Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage1 \n Frame(hold, E_hold)
  hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY source management signature, normal Auth and ST review
  hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  Require inactive role, binding, next attempt_seq and matching predecessor/floors
  hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Atomically reserve journal, quarantine predecessor and enter HELD
  hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Store E_held = E_WB(held, (Scope, EH(E_hold), base_state_seq, D_W))

  ' Step 13
  Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage1 \n Frame(held, E_held) \n Release at the fixed deadline

  ' Step 14
  Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage4 \n Frame(held, E_held)

  alt HELD is authenticated and durably consumed
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY target signature, EH(E_hold), Scope and base sequence
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically record HELD and D_B = D_B OR D_W
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Create n_prev and permutation of 1..193; enter PREVIOUS_PENDING
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Q_prev = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope, 0, 1, space_prev), n_prev)
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Store challenge and E_prev = ENC(k_BS, LCTX(previous_challenge), Q_prev)

    ' Step 15
    Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage4 \n Frame(previous_challenge, E_prev)

    ' Step 16
    Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage2 \n **QR**(Frame(previous_challenge, E_prev))
    hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; validate Scope/round/phase and build five independent display maps

    ' Step 17
    ST o-> User:  <b>ConsentRotationStOutput2 \n **ST's Monitor**(Ask for previous committed set without displaying the answer)

    ' Step 18
    User o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationStInput2 \n **ST's Joystick**(Select five distinct countries)
    hnote over ST #Lavender:  R_prev = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope, 0, 1, original_indices), n_prev)

    ' Step 19
    ST o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationStIsoMessage2 \n **QR**(Frame(previous_answer, ENC(k_SB, LCTX(previous_answer), R_prev)))

    ' Step 20
    Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage5 \n Frame(previous_answer, ENC(k_SB, LCTX(previous_answer), R_prev))
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; check outstanding scope/phase/nonce, five distinct indices and ranges
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Resolve countries; compare all five against committed predecessor
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  D_B = D_B OR mismatch; answer_seq = base_state_seq + 1
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  E_continue = ENC(k_BS, LCTX(previous_result), MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,0,0),n_prev))
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically consume response, persist D_B/answer_seq/cache and enter ENROLLING

    ' Step 21
    Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage5 \n Frame(previous_result, E_continue) \n Release at the fixed deadline

    ' Step 22
    Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage3 \n **QR**(Frame(previous_result, E_continue))
    hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; verify expected Scope and n_prev; continue without correctness feedback

    loop Enrollment round r = 1..3 until READY or cancellation
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Create n_select and fresh space; persist outstanding phase 2
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Q_select = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope,r,2,space_select),n_select)

      ' Step 23
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage6 \n Frame(selection_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(selection_challenge),Q_select))

      ' Step 24
      Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage4 \n **QR**(Frame(selection_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(selection_challenge),Q_select)))
      hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; require Scope/r/phase 2; replace display maps

      ' Step 25
      ST o-> User:  <b>ConsentRotationStOutput3 \n **ST's Monitor**(Choose fresh set)

      ' Step 26
      User o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationStInput3 \n **ST's Joystick**(Select five distinct countries)
      hnote over ST #Lavender:  R_select = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope,r,2,indices),n_select)

      ' Step 27
      ST o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationStIsoMessage3 \n **QR**(Frame(selection_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(selection_answer),R_select)))

      ' Step 28
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage6 \n Frame(selection_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(selection_answer),R_select))
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; validate nonce/count/ranges; resolve and journal candidate selection
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Compute history non-reuse without changing D_B

      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Create n_confirm1 and fresh space; persist outstanding phase 3
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Q1 = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope,r,3,space1),n_confirm1)

      ' Step 29
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage7 \n Frame(confirmation_1_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(confirmation_1_challenge),Q1))

      ' Step 30
      Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage5 \n **QR**(Frame(confirmation_1_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(confirmation_1_challenge),Q1)))
      hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; require Scope/r/phase 3; replace display maps

      ' Step 31
      ST o-> User:  <b>ConsentRotationStOutput4 \n **ST's Monitor**(Reproduce the candidate set)

      ' Step 32
      User o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationStInput4 \n **ST's Joystick**(Select five distinct countries)
      hnote over ST #Lavender:  R1 = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope,r,3,indices),n_confirm1)

      ' Step 33
      ST o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationStIsoMessage4 \n **QR**(Frame(confirmation_1_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(confirmation_1_answer),R1)))

      ' Step 34
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage7 \n Frame(confirmation_1_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(confirmation_1_answer),R1))
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; validate and consume; record first comparison, preserving D_B

      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Create n_confirm2 and fresh space; persist outstanding phase 4
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Q2 = MessageWithNonce(Check(Scope,r,4,space2),n_confirm2)

      ' Step 35
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage8 \n Frame(confirmation_2_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(confirmation_2_challenge),Q2))

      ' Step 36
      Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage6 \n **QR**(Frame(confirmation_2_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(confirmation_2_challenge),Q2)))
      hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; require Scope/r/phase 4; replace display maps

      ' Step 37
      ST o-> User:  <b>ConsentRotationStOutput5 \n **ST's Monitor**(Reproduce the candidate set)

      ' Step 38
      User o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationStInput5 \n **ST's Joystick**(Select five distinct countries)
      hnote over ST #Lavender:  R2 = MessageWithNonce(Answer(Scope,r,4,indices),n_confirm2)

      ' Step 39
      ST o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationStIsoMessage5 \n **QR**(Frame(confirmation_2_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(confirmation_2_answer),R2)))

      ' Step 40
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage8 \n Frame(confirmation_2_answer, ENC(k_SB,LCTX(confirmation_2_answer),R2))
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; validate and consume; record second comparison, preserving D_B
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  result = READY(2) iff valid, unused, and both confirmations match; otherwise RETRY(1)
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Cache E_round = ENC(k_BS,LCTX(round_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,result),n_confirm2))

      ' Step 41
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage9 \n Frame(round_result, E_round) \n Release at the fixed deadline

      ' Step 42
      Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage7 \n **QR**(Frame(round_result, E_round))
      hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; verify Scope/r/n_confirm2 and display candidate result only
    end

    opt Authenticated cancellation, applicable at any precommit ST phase

      ' Step 43
      User o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoInput2 \n REQUEST_CANCEL

      ' Step 44
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage9 \n REQUEST_CANCEL, empty canonical tuple
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Serialize with acceptance; retire pending country challenge; preserve accepted duress
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Store fresh cancel_nonce and Q_cancel = MessageWithNonce(Scope,cancel_nonce)

      ' Step 45
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage10 \n Frame(cancel_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(cancel_challenge),Q_cancel))

      ' Step 46
      Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage8 \n **QR**(Frame(cancel_challenge, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(cancel_challenge),Q_cancel)))
      hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; verify active Scope and nonce

      ' Step 47
      ST o-> User:  <b>ConsentRotationStOutput6 \n **ST's Monitor**(Confirm cancellation)

      ' Step 48
      User o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationStInput6 \n **ST's Joystick**(Approve cancellation)
      hnote over ST #Lavender:  A_cancel = SIG(ST,DOM(st_cancel),Q_cancel)

      ' Step 49
      ST o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationStIsoMessage6 \n **QR**(Frame(cancel_approval,ENC(k_SB,LCTX(cancel_approval),A_cancel)))

      ' Step 50
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage10 \n Frame(cancel_approval,ENC(k_SB,LCTX(cancel_approval),A_cancel))
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY ST signature, Scope and cancel_nonce; atomically consume and record cancelled
    end

    alt Candidate READY and not cancelled
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  C = (Scope,new_set,count+1,32 padded history rows,base+1,base+2,D_B)
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Freeze enrollment and competing operations
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically store C and E_prepare = E_BW(prepare,(C)); enter PREPARE_WAIT

      ' Step 51
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage11 \n Frame(prepare, E_prepare)

      ' Step 52
      Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage2 \n Frame(prepare, E_prepare)
      hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY source signature; require HELD and matching authorization/Scope
      hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  Check complete history prefix, appended new set, non-reuse and sequences
      hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  C_star = C with latch D_W OR C.duress_latched
      hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  E_prepared = E_WB(prepared,(Scope,EH(E_prepare),C_star))
      hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Atomically persist D_W, answer_seq, C_star, E_prepared; enter PREPARED

      ' Step 53
      Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage2 \n Frame(prepared, E_prepared) \n Release at the fixed deadline

      ' Step 54
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage11 \n Frame(prepared, E_prepared)
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY target signature, EH(E_prepare) and all candidate fields
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Permit only OR latch merge; atomically persist C_star and receipt; enter PREPARED
    else Candidate unavailable, third round failed, or cancellation accepted
      hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Keep accepted D_B and quarantine; no commit readiness
    end

    alt Both durable prepares exist and coordinator chooses COMMIT
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  E_commit = E_BW(commit,(Scope,EH(E_prepared),CD(C_star),base+2))
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically install C_star, final sequence, COMMIT decision and exact bytes; enter COMMIT_WAIT

      ' Step 55
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage12 \n Frame(commit, E_commit)

      ' Step 56
      Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage3 \n Frame(commit, E_commit)
      hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY source signature; match EH(E_prepared), CD(C_star), final sequence
      hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  E_committed = E_WB(committed,(Scope,EH(E_commit),CD(C_star),base+2,D_W))
      hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Atomically install C_star and receipt; enter COMPLETE, still inactive

      ' Step 57
      Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage3 \n Frame(committed, E_committed) \n Release at the fixed deadline

      ' Step 58
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage12 \n Frame(committed, E_committed)
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY Scope, EH(E_commit), CD(C_star), sequence and prepared latch
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically retain terminal evidence; clear withdrawal quarantine; enter COMPLETE

      ' Step 59
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage13 \n Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,3),ui_anchor)))

      ' Step 60
      Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage9 \n **QR**(Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,3),ui_anchor))))
      hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; match active Scope/ui_anchor; display completion once
    else Coordinator chooses ABORT before any durable COMMIT
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  checked = journal.has_accepted_previous; final_seq = base + 1 + checked
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  E_abort = E_BW(abort,(Scope,checked,final_seq,D_B))
      hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically record ABORT decision, final sequence and exact bytes; enter ABORT_WAIT

      ' Step 61
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage14 \n Frame(abort, E_abort)

      ' Step 62
      Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage4 \n Frame(abort, E_abort)
      hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY source signature; require HELD or PREPARED, matching Scope and final sequence
      hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  D_W = D_W OR received_latch; E_aborted = E_WB(aborted,(Scope,EH(E_abort),final_seq,D_W))
      hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Atomically retain D_W, quarantine, sequence, attempt floor and exact receipt; enter ABORTED

      ' Step 63
      Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage4 \n Frame(aborted, E_aborted) \n Release at the fixed deadline

      ' Step 64
      Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage13 \n Frame(aborted, E_aborted)
      hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY exact request digest/sequence; persist OR merge and terminal receipt; enter ABORTED
      hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Preserve predecessor quarantine; discard only staged candidate material

      ' Step 65
      Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage15 \n Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,4),ui_anchor)))

      ' Step 66
      Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage10 \n **QR**(Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,r,4),ui_anchor))))
      hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; match Scope/ui_anchor; display cancellation without duress classification
    end

  else HELD is unavailable or unacknowledged
    hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  No previous-set question is issued; previous_checked is false
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  E_abort0 = E_BW(abort_unheld,(Scope,PairCertificate,Auth,base+1,D_B))
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically record ABORT decision, final sequence and exact bytes; enter ABORT_WAIT

    ' Step 67
    Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage16 \n Frame(abort_unheld, E_abort0)

    ' Step 68
    Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage5 \n Frame(abort_unheld, E_abort0) \n even if the earlier HOLD was lost
    hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY source signature, normal authorization, ST review, binding and attempt floor
    hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  Require unseen or HELD; preserve quarantine; D_W = D_W OR received_latch
    hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Atomically record ABORTED, base+1, floor and E_aborted0 = E_WB(aborted,(Scope,EH(E_abort0),base+1,D_W))

    ' Step 69
    Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage5 \n Frame(aborted, E_aborted0) \n Release at the fixed deadline

    ' Step 70
    Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage14 \n Frame(aborted, E_aborted0)
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY Scope/EH(E_abort0)/sequence; persist OR merge and terminal evidence

    ' Step 71
    Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage17 \n Frame(terminal_result, stored ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,0,4),review_nonce)))

    ' Step 72
    Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage11 \n **QR**(Frame(terminal_result, stored \n ENC(k_BS,LCTX(terminal_result),MessageWithNonce(UiResult(Scope,0,4),review_nonce))))
    hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; verify reviewed Scope and review_nonce; display cancellation once
  end
end

group Recovery at any interrupted control boundary
  opt Delivery retry while the bound attempt remains admitted

    ' Step 73
    Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage18 \n Frame(op, E_request) \n Retransmit the exact stored bytes

    ' Step 74
    Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage6 \n Frame(op, E_request) \n Retransmit the exact stored bytes without a new IV or altered candidate
    hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  Match accepted request digest; no repeated state transition or persistent write

    ' Step 75
    Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage6 \n cached_receipt_frame \n Release on this delivery's fixed deadline

    ' Step 76
    Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage15 \n cached_receipt_frame
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Consume idempotently only in the proper decision/receipt handler
  end

  opt Source needs current target evidence
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Reserve query slot; generate fresh query_nonce; store E_query = E_BW(status,(Scope,query_nonce))

    ' Step 77
    Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage19 \n Frame(status, E_query)

    ' Step 78
    Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage7 \n Frame(status, E_query)
    hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY bound attempt and query budget; read durable phase/sequence and terminal evidence
    hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Store E_status = E_WB(status_response,(Scope,EH(E_query),query_nonce,phase,seq,kind,evidence_bytes))

    ' Step 79
    Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage7 \n Frame(status_response, E_status) \n Release at the fixed deadline

    ' Step 80
    Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage16 \n Frame(status_response, E_status)
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY Scope, request digest, fresh query nonce and bounded evidence
    hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Apply terminal evidence and its latch merge through the exact decision/receipt handler
    note over Boomlet, Boomletwo #LightYellow
      PREPARED without a source decision cannot activate the backup.
      Resend exact PREPARE to recover PREPARED; STATUS creates no decision.
      Recover COMMITTED or ABORTED through their normal receipt handlers.
      A source already at COMMIT_WAIT must finish COMMIT, never abort.
    end note
  end

  opt Prepared target needs the source decision
    hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  Reserve query slot; generate fresh target_query_nonce; store E_query2 = E_WB(status,(Scope,target_query_nonce))

    ' Step 81
    Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletwoIsoMessage8 \n Frame(status, E_query2)

    ' Step 82
    Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage17 \n Frame(status, E_query2)
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY current attempt and nonce; select exact durable decision or NONE
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Check query budget; store E_status2 = \n E_BW(status_response,(Scope,EH(E_query2),target_query_nonce,phase,seq,kind,evidence_bytes))

    ' Step 83
    Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage20 \n Frame(status_response, E_status2) \n Release at the fixed deadline

    ' Step 84
    Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletwoMessage8 \n Frame(status_response, E_status2)
    hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  DEC; VERIFY fresh nonce and scope; recover original COMMIT/ABORT envelope through its handler
    note over Boomlet, Boomletwo #LightYellow
      NONE, timeout, missing source, or conflicting evidence leaves authority held.
      No old receipt reconstructs an untransferred latch or proves current eligibility.
    end note
  end
end

group ST restart or terminal-result loss
  hnote over ST #Lavender:  Create fresh ui_query_nonce using retained setup and pair anchors

  ' Step 85
  ST o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationStIsoMessage7 \n **QR**(Frame(ui_status,ENC(k_SB,LCTX(ui_status),MessageWithNonce((setup_id,pair_digest),ui_query_nonce))))

  ' Step 86
  Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoBoomletMessage18 \n Frame(ui_status,ENC(k_SB,LCTX(ui_status),MessageWithNonce((setup_id,pair_digest),ui_query_nonce)))
  hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC; match retained binding; check eight-query budget; read current or last terminal journal
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Retire any unconsumed input nonce; prepare fresh UiResume; preserve accepted duress
  hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Pending cancellation uses phase 5, fresh cancel nonce and identity-space padding
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  E_ui_reply = ENC(k_BS,LCTX(ui_status_response),MessageWithNonce((Scope,ui_status,UiResume),ui_query_nonce))
  hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  Atomically store replacement, query acceptance and exact E_ui_reply

  ' Step 87
  Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>ConsentRotationBoomletIsoMessage21 \n Frame(ui_status_response,E_ui_reply)

  ' Step 88
  Iso o-> ST:  <b>ConsentRotationIsoStMessage12 \n **QR**(Frame(ui_status_response,E_ui_reply))
  hnote over ST #Pink:  DEC; verify its outstanding query nonce and Scope; use only the authenticated UiResume after restart
  hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  Display terminal status once, rebuild country maps, or confirm the resumed cancellation
  note over ST, Boomletwo #LightYellow
    Eight fresh STATUS queries per direction and eight UI queries are reserved per attempt.
    Exact duplicate queries recover cached bytes without writes or nonce replacement.
    Exhaustion stalls fresh queries and preserves decisions, holds and duress.
  end note
end

group Subsequent ordinary withdrawal after rotation completion

  ' Step 89
  User o-> Niso:  <b>ConsentRotationNisoInput1 \n Return eligible active device to Niso for ordinary withdrawal
  note over ST, SAR #LightYellow
    The eligible active device is Boomlet, or Boomletwo after independently proved activation.
    Transaction review, unanimous approvals, digging and signing rules still apply.
    This subflow shows the existing local placeholder path for initial commit and every Ping.
  end note

  loop Initial TxCommit, then every new Ping
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  effective_duress = retained_duress_latched OR current_check_is_duress
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  p = doxing_key_for_sar if effective_duress, otherwise zero_bytes_32
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  P = ENC(k_BSAR,canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_placeholder",approved_id),p), fresh IV
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  inner = SIG(logical_Boomlet,"Boomerang/withdrawal/" + kind, TxCommit_or_Ping)
    hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  outer = SIG(logical_Boomlet,"Boomerang/withdrawal/" + kind + "_envelope",PaddedMessage(inner,P))

    ' Step 90
    Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage1 \n ENC(k_BWT,canonical_encode("withdrawal_" + kind,approved_id),outer)

    ' Step 91
    Niso o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage1 \n ENC(k_BWT,canonical_encode("withdrawal_" + kind,approved_id),outer)
    hnote over WT #Pink:  DEC; verify both signatures, approval/commit gate, approved ID and freshness/sequence

    ' Step 92
    WT o-> SAR:  <b>WithdrawalWtSarMessage1 \n Exact P on existing setup-bound placeholder forwarding path
    hnote over SAR #LavenderBlush:  Set fixed ack_release_at before parsing; authenticate, decrypt and classify P
    hnote over SAR #Lavender:  Construct signed exact-envelope acknowledgment and identical fixed-shape processing record
    hnote over SAR #LavenderBlush:  Durably commit replay tuple (approved_id,logical_Boomlet_pubkey,P.iv); activate duress for new valid duress tuple
    hnote over SAR #Lavender:  Ack = SIG(SAR,"Boomerang/withdrawal/sar_placeholder_response",P)
    hnote over SAR #Lavender:  E_ack = ENC(k_SARB,canonical_encode("withdrawal_sar_placeholder_response",approved_id),Ack)

    ' Step 93
    SAR o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalSarWtMessage1 \n Exact E_ack at the fixed deadline; no late acknowledgment after overrun

    ' Step 94
    WT o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalWtNisoMessage1 \n E_ack with existing verified commit collection or encrypted Pong

    ' Step 95
    Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage1 \n E_ack with existing verified commit collection or encrypted Pong
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  DEC E_ack; verify SAR signature and byte-for-byte Ack.content == P
    hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Verify accompanying withdrawal evidence before any progress
  end

  note over Boomlet, SAR #LightYellow
    Correct answers to the new set cannot override a true persistent latch.
    Every new Ping uses a new placeholder IV; in-flight retries retain exact bytes.
    Safe and duress share message shape, timing, queues, writes, retries and exposed status.
    Rescue work cannot change acknowledgment release or reveal classification to Niso or WT.
    No later traffic means no delivery claim, even though the latch remains durable.
  end note
end
@enduml
